registry defined in Section 10.3.2 of RFC 6350 <xref target="RFC6350" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC6350"/>.</t>
      <dl indent="3" newline="false" spacing="compact" pn="section-4-4">
        <dt pn="section-4-4.1">Namespace:</dt>
        <dd pn="section-4-4.2"/>
        <dt pn="section-4-4.3">Property:</dt>
        <dd pn="section-4-4.4">CC</dd>
        <dt pn="section-4-4.5">Reference:</dt>
        <dd pn="section-4-4.6">Section 3.1 of RFC 8605 (this RFC)</dd>
      </dl>
    </section>
    <section anchor="security-considerations" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-5">
      <name slugifiedName="name-security-considerations">Security Considerations</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-5-1">The CONTACT-URI value is purposefully intended to be a publicly
visible contact reference; as such, it cannot require confidentiality
protection.  There are, however, privacy implications in the choice
of a URI scheme for the web form contact method.  An &quot;https&quot; URI
value can be used to indicate support for confidentiality protection
for connections to the server that publishes the web form.  This
document presents no other security considerations beyond those
described in Section 9 of the base vCard specification <xref target="RFC6350" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC6350"/>.</t>
    </section>
